<title>INDIA: India approves Tate &amp; Lyle subsidiary.</title>
<headline>India approves Tate &amp; Lyle subsidiary.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's Industry Ministry said on Monday it had cleared a proposal by Britain's Tate &amp; Lyle Plc to set up a wholly-owned subsidiary to invest in sugar, cereal, sweetener, starch production and consultancy-related areas.</p>
<p>The holding company, which would be located in the northern Indian state of Uttar Pradesh, will have a foreign direct investment of 700 million rupees ($19.6 million), the ministry said in a statement.</p>
<p>($1=35.70 rupees)</p>
</text>
